       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg is a toxic dose, not a high therapeutic one. No indication supports it, and 70 kg adults have had serious toxicity at much lower amounts. Entering it as a routine daily order would put the patient at real risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmia.\n\nYou may have a reason I can't see. If so, these routes are safer:\n- **Pharmacy or psychiatry consult.** A pharmacist or psychiatrist can review the dose and, if it's justified, enter it with the safeguards that go with it.\n- **Toxicology or Poison Control (1-800-222-1222).** Call them if this is meant to address an unusual situation.\n- **A different dose.** I can enter sertraline within the labeled range, up to 200 mg once daily, right now. I can also enter a dose titration.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
